## Project layout

```
{{projectName}}/
├── frontend/        # React + Vite + TypeScript
├── backend/         # Django 5 + DRF (Python 3.13)
│   ├── config/         # project: settings/ (base|local|production), urls, wsgi
│   └── apps/           # one Django app per domain
│       ├── core/       # health endpoint{{#if withCelery}}, example Celery tasks{{/if}}
│       ├── users/      # custom User model + read-only API
{{#if withS3}}
│       ├── files/      # uploads on S3/MinIO (presigned URLs)
{{/if}}
│       └── <app>/      # models, serializers, services, views, urls, tests/
├── e2e/             # Playwright + Cucumber end-to-end suite
├── docs/            # MkDocs documentation site
└── docker-compose.yml
```

Each app follows the same convention: **serializers list fields explicitly,
views declare permissions and delegate writes to `services.py`, every model
change ships its migration, every app ships tests** — enforced by `dude lint`
(see `.claude/rules/BE/`).

## Quick start — local (no Docker)

```bash
# Frontend (terminal 1)
cd frontend
pnpm install
pnpm dev          # http://localhost:5173

# Backend (terminal 2)
cd backend
uv sync
uv run python manage.py migrate
uv run python manage.py runserver   # http://localhost:8000
```
